-- title:
--   Far component of the geometric special fibre descends to ̄ k₀
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, containing a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137), that is, the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the rational function field of $X_1(Mp)$ inside Laurent series over $L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) transported along [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229), the pushout of the two affine charts attached to the subalgebras `chartAlgFin A K j` and `chartAlgInf A K j`, with structure morphism $\pi_X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $U \subseteq X$ be an open subscheme over which $\pi_X$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and which contains every such open subscheme, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $\pi_X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ whose image lies in $U$. Put $k_0 = \overline{A/\mathfrak{m}}$, the algebraic closure of the residue field of $A$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and $\iota_0 : k_0 \to k$ a ring homomorphism; write $X_k$ and $X_{k_0}$ for the pullbacks of $\pi_X$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $A \to k_0 \to k$ and of $A \to k_0$. Assume given closed immersions $i_1 : C_1 \to X_k$, $i_2 : C_2 \to X_k$ with $C_1, C_2$ irreducible, such that every point of $X_k$ lies in the range of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the point of $X_k$ determined by $\varepsilon$ (via `sectionFibrePoint`, evaluated at the closed point of $k$) lies in the range of $i_1$ but not of $i_2$, and the range of $i_2$ is not contained in that of $i_1$; and closed immersions $j_1 : D_1 \to X_{k_0}$, $j_2 : D_2 \to X_{k_0}$ over geometrically integral structure morphisms $d_1, d_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k_0$ (compatibly, $j_\nu$ followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} k_0$ being $d_\nu$), satisfying the same three conditions over $k_0$. Then the canonical base-change morphism $X_k \to X_{k_0}$ induced by the identity on $X$ and by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\iota_0$ maps the range of $i_2$ onto exactly the range of $j_2$.
--
--   This identifies the component of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ not met by the given section with the base change of the corresponding component over the algebraic closure of the residue field: under the stated hypotheses the two closed subsets in each case are the irreducible components, and the far ones correspond. It is used in the analysis of the modular units and degeneration of the special fibre of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$.
